---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const a='/equipment/09-09/', product='https://www.keysight.com/us/en/product/E36313A/160w-triple-output-power-supply-6v-10a-2x-25v-2a.html',ds='https://www.keysight.com/us/en/assets/7018-05629/data-sheets/5992-2124.pdf',ug='https://www.keysight.com/us/en/assets/9018-04576/user-manuals/9018-04576.pdf',old='https://www.mouser.com/pdfDocs/E36311-90001.pdf',pic='https://www.keysight.com/content/dam/keysight/en/img/prd/generators-sources-power/power-supplies/bench/36300/E36313A-TRANSP-1600x900.png';
const panels=[['front','Front elevation','Model-specific E36313A product photo: yellow, green and blue channel groups, 4.3 in display, On keys, separate voltage and current knobs and six 4 mm sockets. The three positive jacks sit at about 35%, 63% and 81% of fascia width from the left edge in both the straight-on photo and model; this is a placement check, not a factory drawing.',pic],['posts','Output connections','User’s Guide, front-panel connections: three independent pairs and a separate earth post. Banana plugs, short leads and a passive load bank are original virtual accessories, not stock hardware.',ug+'#page=26'],['rear','Rear elevation','Compare the E36312A/13A-family rear-panel image (User’s Guide p. 16; 2018 ed. p. 17). Output/sense terminals, fan, digital I/O, LAN, USB-B, mains and selector are present. This configuration has an unpopulated GPIB bay; connector centers are inferred.',old+'#page=17'],['body','Chassis and working area','The family photograph on p. 1 establishes the long metal body behind the dark front. Envelope dimensions are specified; side perforation pattern, foot positions, strap and all accessory lengths are reconstructed, not measured.','https://assets-us-01.kc-usercontent.com/ecb176a6-5a2e-0000-8943-84491e5fc8d1/1f070646-29a3-451b-8fd0-cf2faf83408e/Keysight%20E36300%20Series%20Product%20Fact%20Sheet.pdf#page=1']];
const specs=[['CH1 / CH2 / CH3','6 V × 10 A / 25 V × 2 A / 25 V × 2 A','Limits for each enabled isolated channel. Rated power sum 160 W. No negative rail on this model.',ds+'#page=15','Datasheet, model table'],['Net W × H × D','213 × 133 × 364 mm','Geometry without feet, strap or GPIB. Coordinates derive from the complete model, not a single box.',ds+'#page=15','Datasheet p. 15'],['Overall W × H × D / mass','216 × 145 × 367 mm; 9.8 kg','With feet and strap. Optional GPIB is not included; mass is not simulated.',ds+'#page=15','Datasheet p. 15'],['Display','4.3 in diagonal, color LCD','Active window and colored readback groups; physical controls scaled from front photograph.',ug+'#page=13','Guide p. 13 and product image'],['Remote sense','1 V maximum in a load lead','Behavior: model assumes the loop resistance is split equally between the outbound and return lead. Software also imposes rated terminal-voltage ceiling as a conservative headroom limit.',ds+'#page=13','Datasheet: supplemental characteristics'],['Sense topology','local 2-wire or remote 4-wire','Remote voltage feedback is at the load; current limiting is unchanged. The rear terminal blocks accommodate separate sense connections.',ug+'#page=31','Guide, 4-wire sense'],['Console revision','E36313A; standard LAN + USB-B; no GPIB','Do not confuse with E36311A (± rail) or E36312A (80 W). No series/parallel, sequencing hardware, timing or noise model.',product,'Keysight product']];
---
<Layout pageTitle="Precision power supply laboratory" subtitle="" description="Explore voltage regulation, current limiting and remote sensing on a metric E36313A bench." wide={true}>
<article id="psu09" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/09-09/">← Equipment 09-09</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#sources">Reference sheet</a><a href="#checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">09-09 / ELECTRICAL INSTRUMENTATION</span><h2>Where a voltage source becomes a current source</h2><p class="eq-lede">CH1 is set to 5 V with a 100 mA limit. A 100 Ω load draws only 50 mA. Switch it to 10 Ω: the same instrument must lower its voltage to 1 V. Operate the Keysight E36313A directly or use the control panel.</p></header>
<div class="p-grid"><section><p class="eq-meta">01 / INSTRUMENT</p><h3>Three-output E36313A</h3><canvas id="p-model" aria-label="Rotatable E36313A with front panel, terminals and passive loads"></canvas><div class="p-tools">{[['home','Reset view'],['front','Front'],['posts','Binding posts'],['rear','Rear'],['body','Body']].map(([k,t])=><button data-camera={k}>{t}</button>)}</div><p id="p-modelstatus" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom. Click the colored channel-select key, its On key, or a binding post or plug. The two rotary controls adjust voltage and current limit; Shift-click turns them back. Selected output, cable visibility, meter and desk readout share the same state.</p></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">02 / WORKING CIRCUIT</p><h3>Supply and load</h3><div class="p-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Inspect a channel">{[1,2,3].map(i=><button data-ch={i-1}>CH{i}</button>)}</div><form id="p-form"><label>Voltage setpoint (V)<input type="number" step="any" min="0" id="p-volts" /></label><label>Current limit (A)<input type="number" step="any" min="0" id="p-limit" /></label><label>Load resistance (Ω)<input type="number" step="any" min="0" max="10000000" id="p-ohm" /></label><label>Lead-loop resistance (Ω)<input type="number" step="any" min="0" max="100" id="p-lead" /></label><label>Sensing<select id="p-sense"><option value="local">Local / two-wire</option><option value="remote">Remote / four-wire</option></select></label><label>Remote sense pair<select id="p-pair"><option value="closed">Intact</option><option value="open">Disconnected</option></select></label></form><div class="p-tools"><button id="p-output">Output</button><button id="p-plug">Load</button><button id="p-all">All outputs On/Off</button></div><div class="p-tools"><button id="p-cv">100 Ω · CV example</button><button id="p-cc">10 Ω · CC example</button><button id="p-remote">Remote-sense example</button><button id="p-reset">Restore bench</button></div><p id="p-msg" aria-live="polite"></p></section></div>
<section><p class="eq-meta">03 / SIMULATED MEASUREMENTS</p><h3>What reaches each load?</h3><div class="p-scroll"><table><thead><tr>{['Channel','State','Meter V','Terminal V','Load V','Current mA','Load W','Lead W'].map(x=><th>{x}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody id="p-rows"></tbody></table></div><p id="p-total" aria-live="polite"></p><p>Open means no connected specimen; load voltage is undefined (—), not a measured zero. OFF is a different state. The readback represents an ideal calculation, not physical instrument accuracy.</p>
<div class="p-tools"><button id="p-csv">Export readings CSV</button><button id="p-json">Export run JSON</button><button id="p-bank">Save load configuration</button></div>
<label class="p-import">Import a saved load configuration <input id="p-upload" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"/></label><a href={a+'example-load-bank.json'} download>Example input</a> · <a href={a+'example-result.json'}>Example result</a> · <a href={a+'schema.json'}>I/O contract</a></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">04 / OUTPUT TO ANOTHER STATION</p><h3>Load-step log</h3><p>With the selected output enabled and connected, log a hypothetical passive load change from R to R/10 at 5 s and back to R at 10 s, over a 16 s window. Voltage samples are synthetic settled-state plateaus at 10 S/s, not measured transients or a device sequencing feature. Export preserves the load ID, terminal ID, volts, seconds and source settings.</p><div class="p-tools"><button id="p-wave">Export load-step waveform</button><a href={a+'example-waveform.json'} download>5 → 1 → 5 V example</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/09-04/simulator/">Open digital oscilloscope</a></div><p>Import that waveform into the <a href="/simulations/equipment/09-04/">digital oscilloscope</a>, choose a rising 3 V trigger and use the initial framing. The reconstructed return crossing is compared against the known 10 s input step below; the coarse source clock limits timing interpretation.</p></section>
<section id="sources"><p class="eq-meta">05 / INSTRUMENT EVIDENCE</p><h3>Reference sheet</h3><p>All four panels below are original renders of our GLB, not Keysight photographs or CAD. Compare the linked original image or manual to see which details are independently documented.</p><div class="p-refs">{panels.map(([file,title,note,url])=><figure><img src={a+file+'.webp'} loading="lazy" width="750" height="480" alt={'Original model: '+title}/><figcaption><b>{title}.</b> {note} <a href={url}>Reference</a></figcaption></figure>)}</div><div class="p-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Quantity</th><th>Value</th><th>Role and limits</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{specs.map(([q,v,why,url,title])=><tr><th>{q}</th><td>{v}</td><td>{why}</td><td><a href={url}>{title}</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="checks"><p class="eq-meta">06 / EVIDENCE AND LIMITS</p><h3>DC load-line model</h3><p>For two-wire sensing the CV candidate is I* = Vset/(Rload + Rloop). For a valid four-wire circuit it is I* = Vset/Rload. The delivered current is min(I*, Ilimit); Vload = I Rload and Vterminal = I(Rload + Rloop). The software treats an exact tie separately. The output, load and wire powers are Vterminal I, I²Rload and I²Rloop. A short and an open circuit use explicit limiting cases.</p><p>Inputs: three independent, floating positive outputs, 0–10 MΩ passive loads, 0–100 Ω total lead resistance and optional ideal sense pairs. Loads and leads have no thermal dynamics. The remote-sense circuit is conceptual; rear sockets are modeled but sense leads are not animated. A missing sense pair blocks measurement here; the real unit can fall back to local sensing, which is not modeled. No transient, noise, vendor readback uncertainty, OVP/OCP dynamics, power sequencing or protective-earth wiring is simulated. Do not interpret it as operational safety guidance.</p>
<div class="p-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Reference</th><th>Computed</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody id="p-tests"></tbody></table></div><p>Analytical verification and geometry checks, not comparison to an independent physical measurement. <a href={a+'acceptance.md'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Full test report</a> · <a href={a+'interop.json'}>Oscilloscope interoperability</a></p>
<div class="p-tools"><a href={a+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a><a href={a+'e36313a.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a><a href={a+'supply.mjs'}>Solver / VR adapter</a><a href={a+'vr-manifest.json'}>Stable IDs, hit bounds and triangle budget</a></div><p>The GLB and input-independent actions can be mounted in a VR laboratory. Desktop/mobile behavior is also available without WebGL, but this is not an immersive session or a Quest performance claim.</p></section></article></Layout>
